  "narrative": "This batch decomposes the three previously accepted dataset-specific binary associations among feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037. All returned estimates are already signed to the hypothesis direction, so a positive value supports the claimed direction. H54 and H55 test feature_010 present versus absent within feature_002 absent and feature_002 present, respectively. The signed estimates are +0.800 (95% interval +0.744 to +0.857) and +0.878 (+0.773 to +0.982), with adequate cells. Both far exceed the 0.15-unit threshold and lower bounds are well above threshold, so I accept them. H56 and H57 test feature_002 present versus absent within feature_010 absent and present. They are +0.780 (+0.719 to +0.841) and +0.857 (+0.755 to +0.960), respectively, and are also accepted. H58-H62 test feature_037 present versus absent in claimed negative direction; because the returned values are positive, the underlying raw feature_037-present-minus-absent contrasts are negative, consistent with H53. The estimates range from +0.796 to +0.833 with lower bounds at least +0.739 and all intervals clearly above threshold, so I accept them. H60 and H61 test feature_010 and feature_002 within feature_037 absent and are +0.828 and +0.809, respectively, both accepted. H62-H64 test each label in eligibility sets where the other two accepted labels are absent; estimates are +0.814, +0.804, and +0.784, with lower bounds +0.768, +0.757, and +0.736. These results strongly support that, within this dataset, the three binary associations are not merely artifacts of simple co-occurrence or overlap with one another: each persists with very large magnitude even when the other accepted labels are absent. H65 tests a pairwise interaction for feature_010 by feature_002 in the claimed positive direction. The signed estimate is +0.077 with interval -0.042 to +0.196. This is below the 0.15 threshold, not credibly positive, and consistent with approximate additivity of the two positive-label associations. I reject H65 and close that interaction investigation, while noting that a small sub-threshold interaction cannot be ruled out. Important limitations remain: these are marginal stratified contrasts, not a full multivariable or causal model; conditioning on correlated opaque labels could induce associations not intended as causal adjustments; and the predictors may still be proxies for an unmeasured latent structure. The claims remain descriptive associations in this dataset only. Multiplicity is not a major concern for the accepted effects because their point estimates and lower bounds are more than five times the threshold, although the claims are overlapping stratified analyses from the same sample. No independent validation is requested for these decisive conditional effects; validation is better reserved for borderline claims such as the earlier feature_063 effect.",
  "research_notes": "Conditional decomposition of feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 is complete for the registered pairwise and mutually-absent analyses. Each accepted label remains associated with a ~0.78-0.88 signed unit difference in the claimed direction in strata of the other labels and in eligibility sets where the other two labels are absent. The feature_010 by feature_002 interaction H65 is small and not threshold-supported, supporting approximate additivity among positive labels. Interpretation remains dataset-specific and descriptive; no causal or biological interpretation is warranted, and conditioning on correlated labels should not be read as multivariable adjustment. Next priorities: finish any remaining pairwise interactions involving feature_037 if desired, then examine effect modification by feature_040, age, and research signatures, while retaining broad categorical screens H74-H76. Validation is not needed for the current accepted conditional claims because intervals are far beyond threshold."
