  "narrative": "All new estimates are signed to their registered directions. H120, H123, H125, and H126 are strong threshold-supported direct feature_063 contrasts: signed +0.546 when feature_038 is high, +0.454 when feature_018 is low, +0.294 when feature_036 is low, and +0.849 in the predicted joint feature_038-high/feature_018-low stratum. Their 95% intervals lie entirely above 0.15, so I accept these dataset-specific subgroup associations. H121 and H122 are not threshold-supported: feature_038-low gives a near-null opposite-signed effect, and feature_018-high is a tiny positive signed estimate whose interval crosses null and includes values below threshold. H127 is also not threshold-supported and is opposite the registered direction, consistent with attenuation when feature_038 is low and feature_018 is high. H117 is not supported for feature_036 modification; it is signed in the opposite direction and has an interval including zero. H124 is suggestive because feature_036-high has a point estimate above threshold, but its lower bound is below 0.15, so I leave it unresolved and defer it rather than treat it as established. H128 strongly supports that the feature_038 interaction persists after restricting to participants without feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037, reducing the concern that this modification is an artifact of the accepted large binary associations. H129 similarly supports the reversed feature_018 interaction in the clean stratum, but its lower bound is just below threshold, so I keep it unresolved while active. The emerging structure is that the negative feature_063 association is concentrated in feature_038-high and feature_018-low settings and attenuated in their complements. Multiplicity and selection after initial interaction discovery are real concerns; therefore I request independent validation of H119, the unvalidated reversed feature_018 interaction central to this structure. I register the missing feature_038/feature_018 joint cell