  "narrative": "New validation closes the central feature_038/feature_018 follow-up. H136 tests the clean direct feature_063 present-minus-absent contrast in the feature_038-high/feature_018-low cell. Its discovery estimate was +0.839 with a 95% interval of +0.721 to +0.957, and independent validation gave +0.782 with an adjusted interval of +0.667 to +0.897. Both estimates and intervals are far above the 0.15-unit threshold in the registered direction. I therefore keep H136 accepted and close the investigation. H146 tests the clean conditional feature_018-by-feature_063 interaction within feature_038-high cells. Discovery was +0.536 with interval +0.349 to +0.722; validation gave +0.639 with adjusted interval +0.336 to +0.942. The validation is same-signed and strongly threshold-supported, independently confirming that high feature_018 attenuates the feature_063 lower-outcome association inside feature_038-high cells. I keep H146 accepted and close it. Revised central synthesis. The strongest reproducible pattern is that feature_063 presence is associated with lower outcome_001, but this association is not homogeneous across the standardized assay geometry. It is strongest when feature_038 is high and feature_018 is low, moderately attenuated when feature_018 is high, and absent when feature_038 is low. The clean feature_038-high direct contrast is strongly supported (H132: +0.576, +0.462 to +0.689), whereas the clean feature_038-low direct contrast is null (H134: -0.020, -0.089 to +0.049). The validated attenuation interaction (H146) plus the validated strongest-cell direct effect (H136) make the feature_038/feature_018 concentration robust within the supplied dataset. The overall feature_063 effect is also supported: overall H49 is validated (+0.273, +0.133 to +0.412), and the clean all-label-absent stratum is threshold-validated (H93: +0.285, +0.157 to +0.412). These are associations with a composite dependency score, not causal effects and not claims about generalizable biological mechanism. Supported findings. First, the collinear binary label cluster feature_010 and feature_002 shows very large positive signed associations with outcome_001, generally around +0.78 to +0.90; this supports an association cluster but does not decompose their independent contributions. Second, feature_037 presence is associated with much lower outcome_001, with large accepted reverse-direction estimates around +0.80. Third, feature_063 presence is associated with lower outcome_001 overall and is strongly concentrated by feature_038 high and feature_018 low status, with attenuation by feature_018 high. Fourth, feature_036 does not meaningfully modify the feature_063 association: the clean feature_036 interaction is null (H117 and H148), and the feature_038-high direct association remains large in both feature_036-high and feature_036-low subsets. Negative findings. The constructed binary research markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 show no meaningful overall association with outcome_001, and their simple two-way interactions are null or not supported. The validated nulls include H12 and H73, and the original nulls include H11, H29, H30, H15, H27, and H28. Many other registered contrasts are below threshold or not supported, including feature_059 and several categorical contrasts in feature_046, feature_052, feature_061, and feature_062. Clean feature_038-low and feature_038-low/feature_018-low cells do not support a meaningful feature_063 effect. Unresolved uncertainty remains. H137 direct clean feature_038-high/feature_018-high contrast was directionally supported but attenuated on validation, with the adjusted interval below threshold at its lower end, so its threshold-level magnitude remains uncertain. H115 and H119 are accepted as dataset-specific directional findings but validation intervals are too wide or too low to secure threshold-level magnitudes. H141, H129, and H143 are near-threshold or imprecise and remain suggestive rather than established. Accepted active label-positive feature_038-high cells H153 and H155 are large but have small exposed cells and are not independent contributions. H160 age-under-60 is accepted but threshold-uncertain because the lower bound is near the threshold; H158 low log_pfs and H159 age-60-plus remain unresolved. Invalid exact continuous comparisons (for example H37, H38, H39, and H41) are specification failures, not negative evidence. All conclusions remain descriptive associations in the supplied dataset, with residual multiple-testing and confounding risk. Most informative next analysis. With H146 and H136 now independently validated, the central attenuation geometry is robust. The next most decision-relevant validation is H145, the clean conditional feature_038 interaction within feature_018-high cells. It would test whether feature_038-high status retains a threshold-supported feature_063 contrast after feature_018 attenuation, complementing validated H136 in the feature_018-low cell and validated H146 as an interaction. A robust H145 result would strengthen the reciprocal feature_038/feature_018 interpretation; an attenuated or null result would localize the uncertainty to the feature_018-high stratum and would downgrade threshold-level claims for H145 and possibly the high-high direct cell. Secondary is H142, the non-clean analogue of the feature_018 interaction, to test robustness to the large collinear labels.",
  "research_notes": "Updated. H136 and H146 are now independently validated and closed accepted. H136 clean feature_038-high/feature_018-low direct feature_063 contrast is very strong. H146 clean feature_018 attenuation of feature_063 within feature_038-high is robust. Central accepted dataset model: feature_063 presence associated with lower outcome_001; strongest in feature_038-high/feature_018-low, attenuated in feature_018-high, absent in feature_038-low. Large collinear labels feature_010/feature_002 high and feature_037 low remain robust. feature_036 modification is null; direct residual feature_036 contrasts are accepted but threshold-uncertain. Negative findings remain strong for binary markers feature_007/058/015 and many simple interactions. Unresolved threshold uncertainty: H137 attenuated validation lower below threshold; H115/H119 direction only; H141/H129/H143 near threshold; H158/H159 unresolved; H153/H155 small exposed cells; H160 near threshold. Next validation if possible: H145 clean feature_038 interaction within feature_018-high, secondary H142 non-clean analogue. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable."
}

