  "narrative": "All new estimates are already signed to the registered claim direction. For the feature_063 direct contrasts inside feature_038-high cells, H161 through H165 were all positive and threshold-supported, indicating that feature_063 presence remains associated with lower outcome_001 in feature_038-high settings across both age and log_pfs splits. H162, H164, and H165 have intervals well above 0.15 units, so I accept and close those exact marginal associations. H161 is also threshold-supported, but its exposed cell has only 28 observations and the interval is wide; I accept it as a dataset-specific association but keep it active because small-cell instability and residual confounding remain relevant. The corresponding interaction tests H163 and H166 are not threshold-supported: H163 estimate 0.059 with interval crossing zero and H166 estimate 0.111 with interval from -0.174 to 0.447. I reject them as evidence for meaningful age or log_pfs modification within feature_038-high, while noting that the intervals are wide enough that modest modification cannot be excluded. The H167 through H172 results show that feature_037, feature_010, and feature_002 retain very large signed associations with outcome_001 in both feature_038-high and feature_038-low strata. These estimates are far above threshold, so I accept and close the exact comparisons. This contrasts with the feature_063 pattern, where the association is strongly concentrated in feature_038-high cells and largely absent in feature_038-low cells. The new results therefore reinforce that the feature_063 effect is condition-specific whereas the collinear binary-label associations are broadly present across feature_038 levels. Caveats remain: many feature_063 clinical splits are not label-clean and can be confounded by feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037; the subgroup analyses are selected and multiplicity remains a concern. I request validation of H145 because it is the clean conditional feature_038-by-feature_063 interaction within feature_018-high cells, directly complementing validated H136 and H146 and most relevant to whether feature_038 retains a threshold-supported feature_063 contrast after feature_018 attenuation. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations with a composite dependency score, not causal effects or generalizable biological claims.",
  "research_notes": "Updated central pattern. The reproducible feature_063 finding remains: feature_063 presence is associated with lower outcome_001 overall, but the association is concentrated in feature_038-high cells and strongest in feature_038-high/feature_018-low cells; feature_018-high attenuates it; feature_038-low is null. Validation of H136 and H146 made the core feature_038/feature_018 geometry robust. New H161-H165 broad feature_038-high direct contrasts by age and log_pfs are threshold-supported, though some are unclean for collinear labels and H161 has small exposed n; no meaningful age or log_pfs interaction is supported by H163/H166. The collinear label cluster feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 remains strongly associated with outcome_001 and its associations persist across both feature_038-high and feature_038-low strata, supporting distinct label-cluster association patterns rather than concentration like feature_063. Active validation request: H145, the clean conditional feature_038 interaction within feature_018-high cells, to resolve reciprocal attenuation. Remaining uncertainty includes feature_018-high direct effect magnitude, small-cell subgroup estimates, clean low-log_pfs and age-60-plus feature_063 effects, and the inability to decompose collinear label associations into independent contributions. All conclusions remain supplied-dataset descriptive associations, not causal or generalizable mechanisms.",
  "validate": "H145"
