  "narrative": "The new results sharpen the feature_063 structure. H175, H176, H177, H181, H182, H183, and H184 are threshold-supported because their 95% lower bounds exceed 0.15 in the registered signed direction; I accept them. H174's lower bound is just above threshold at 0.192, so I also accept it as a dataset-specific reciprocal feature_038 interaction within feature_018-high after feature_037 is absent. H178 is rejected because feature_063 in feature_038-low under feature_037 absence is near null. H173, H179, and H180 remain unresolved: high-high point estimates are positive and compatible with meaningful effects, but lower bounds fall below 0.15 and exposed cells are small, and residual confounding by the collinear label cluster is plausible. I keep H173, H179, and H180 active. H185 and H186 are deferred as lower-priority small-cell refinements, and H145 is deferred because larger feature_037-absent interactions H174 and H176 now provide stronger evidence for the same reciprocal interaction structure. Multiplicity remains substantial, thresholds are post hoc cuts, and all results are supplied-dataset associations only; the feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 labels cannot be causally separated. No validation was requested because no new voluntary validation requests remain.",
