 H208, H212, H219, H220, H226, H229, H230, H255, H263). Fourth, negative findings are extensive: the explicitly described research markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 do not support threshold contrasts; feature_003, feature_016, feature_053, and most other tested low-prevalence binary or categorical comparisons are rejected or below threshold. Some accepted discovery claims are not independently threshold-confirmed, including overall feature_063 H49 and interaction H115, and several refinements such as H137/H145 remain unresolved because validation intervals cross or miss the threshold. Remaining uncertainty concerns exact threshold geometry: the feature_063 contrast in near-zero feature_038 and moderate feature_018 bands is borderline (H264 and H242), feature_027 near-zero feature_038 and higher feature_018 cutpoints are not fully specified, feature_027 modification by feature_038 or feature_018 is not resolved, and numeric predictor slopes and many categorical levels remain deferred. The most informative next analyses are the four registered focused conditional separability/cutpoint tests plus existing H269/H270: after excluding the opposite lower-score marker, test whether feature_027 persists in the feature_038 near-zero band and in high feature_018, and whether feature_063 persists in the feature_038 near-zero band and the moderate feature_018 band. These should be interpreted only as supplied-dataset associations, with post-hoc threshold selection, high multiplicity, opaque correlated predictors, and no causal, mechanistic, biomarker, or generalizability claim.",
