re association that is not merely an artifact of excluding feature_063 in this specific region. However, exposed n=26, conditional selection, and opaque correlated predictors require caution; the conclusion remains a dataset-specific association.\n\nH304 is accepted and closed. In the clean label-cluster setting feature_010=0, feature_002=0, feature_037=0, the feature_063 lower-score contrast remains threshold-supported when extended to feature_018<=0.5 with feature_038>=0: signed +0.794, interval +0.702 to +0.886, cells 42/291. This supports the pattern that feature_063=1 is associated with more negative scores in positive feature_038 with low-to-moderate feature_018, but it does not locate an exact boundary and remains a discovery-only band selection.\n\nH84-H88 are rejected and closed. These tests of whether standardized signatures feature_038, feature_018, or feature_036 modify the large label-cluster effects produced small signed estimates that are not threshold-supported: H84 +0.044, H85 +0.093, H86 -0.053, H87 +0.032, and H88 +0.060. Their intervals either include zero or, where upper bounds extend modestly above threshold, do not provide evidence of a scientifically meaningful interaction. These results do not establish feature_038/feature_018/feature_036 moderation of feature_010, feature_002, or feature_037 associations.\n\nH17 and H18 are rejected and closed. Feature_014 versus its comparator, direction +1, is near null and not threshold-supported: signed -0.029, interval -0.124 to +0.066. Feature_021 versus its comparator, direction -1, is also near null and not threshold-supported: signed +0.031, interval -0.045 to +0.107. These common binary contrasts do not show meaningful association with outcome_001 in the supplied dataset.\n\nNo validation request is made because the remaining voluntary validation budget is zero. The strongest new conclusion is that the feature_010/feature_002/feature_037 label-cluster pattern persists inside the feature_063=1 subg